  "claim": "The parliament type that uses the procedure referred to as \"Laying before the house\", was modeled after the United Kingdom and is also used in Canada since 1892.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Constitution of Alberta. Sentence: The Constitution of Alberta describes the fundamental rules under which the Canadian province of Alberta is governed.\nPage: Constitution of Alberta. Sentence: As is typical of all Canadian provinces, and Westminster systems more generally, Alberta's is an unwritten constitution.\nPage: Westminster system. Sentence: The Westminster system is a parliamentary system of government modelled after that which developed in the United Kingdom.\nPage: Laying before the house. Sentence: In parliamentary procedure, especially the Westminster system, a document is laid before the house or Laid on the Table of the House when it is formally recognised as having been made available for members of a deliberative assembly to read.",
